Testing math ceiling function (kor):
\nPositive numbers:
  kor(4.2) = 5
  kor(5.8) = 6
  kor(9.01) = 10
\nIntegers:
  kor(7) = 7
  kor(0) = 0
\nNegative numbers:
  kor(-3.7) = -3
  kor(-1.2) = -1
  kor(-8.999) = -8
\nEdge cases:
  kor(0.1) = 1
  kor(-0.1) = 0
  kor(0.999) = 1
\nComparison with daji (floor):
  Value 1: 7.3
  daji(value1) = 7
  kor(value1) = 8
  Value 2: -2.6
  daji(value2) = -3
  kor(value2) = -2
\nWith variables:
  x = 6.2
  y = -4.8
  kor(x) = 7
  kor(y) = -4
\nPractical examples:
  17 items with containers of size 5 = 4 containers needed
  30 results with 8 per page = 4 pages needed
\nMath ceiling tests completed!
